.TH AD_ANNOTATE 1 "2026-09-03" "ad 2.0" "ad tools"
.SH NAME
ad_annotate \- add context comments to ops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_annotate
<oldfile> <newfile> < ops.tsv > annotated.tsv
.br
.B ad_annotate
--help | -h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_annotate
reads ops from stdin, simulates the buffer state, and inserts comment
lines showing the text content before and after each bundle of delete
or insert ops. Keep bundles (2+ consecutive) get a summary comment.
Single keeps and \\n keeps get no comment.
.PP
This is called automatically by
.BR ad_gen_ops (1)
when the
.B --annotate
flag is used.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
# old: <full old line>        ← before each HUNK
# new: <full new line>
# keep: "text" (line N, cols X-Y)  ← before keep bundles (2+)
# old: "line before"          ← before delete bundles
# new: "line after"
# old: "line before"          ← before insert bundles
# new: "line after"
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Direct usage:
.B ad_annotate old.py new.py < ops.tsv > annotated.tsv
.TP
Through ad_gen_ops:
.B ad_gen_ops old.py new.py --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --annotate > ops.tsv
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_gen_ops (1),
.BR ad_session (1),
.BR ad (1)
